<p>Los Angeles is expensive, sprawling and full of people chasing the same opportunities, which is exactly why the best side hustles in Los Angeles are the ones that lean into what only LA has: an entertainment industry that hires by the day, a calendar of sold-out stadium nights, millions of dog owners and homeowners who pay well for convenience, and a creator economy that needs editors, shooters and assistants. Pick the right lane and a side gig here can cover a real chunk of rent.</p>
<p>This guide walks through 16 side gigs in Los Angeles that work right now, what each typically pays, what it costs to start, which neighborhoods to target and the California tax and license rules you need to know before your first invoice.</p>

